\title{Proving that a function is not surjective}
\date{2026-03-10T10:59:39Z}
\tag{discrete}
\taxon{Remark}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{To show something is \em{not} [onto / surjective](00A9), we just have to show the negation:}

  \stmt{\neg (\forall b \in B \st \exists a \in A \st f(a) = b)}
  \reason{\equiv}{De Morgan }
  \stmt{\exists b \in B \st \forall a \in A \st f(a) \neq b.}

\p{That is, “there is some #{b \in B} which is not the output of #{f} for any #{a
\in A}”.}
